president-elect macron has confirmed the  withdrawal of french troops from mali  after 10 years macron denied the french  mission in mali ended in failure but he  accused mali's transitional government  of forcing french troops to pull out  france and european allies will continue  what they call a joint action against  terrorism in the sahara region  we cannot stay engaged militarily next  to authorities who do not share our  strategy nor our objectives that's the  situation we are confronted by in mali  today  in these conditions france and its  partners in this fight against terrorism  and the states participating in the  takuba task force have taken the  decision to remove military forces from  mali this removal will begin by the  closure of bases in gosi menaka and gao  it will be ordered with the malian  military forces and the u.n forces in  mali  during this period we will maintain our  mission in support for the un  peacekeeping mission as well  for us at monetary events from senegal's  capital of dhaka and nasa to tell us  more about this announcement and its  implications  yeah we thought that this would happen  the relations with mali have really  suffered uh since the military coup just  lost at the end of last month the french  ambassador was given 72 hours to leave  the country that's after the french  foreign minister had called the military  junta in mali illegitimate now there is  increasing anti-french sentiment in the  region especially in mali there were  celebrations on the street when the  ambassador was told to leave so the  situation for france has changed now  what emmanuel macron has just said that  they will be uh having a coordinated uh  withdrawal from the north first and this  could take four to six months but now he  also said that the center for this fight  against terrorism as they call it will  now be niger now france does have  a  presence in west africa in some of the  neighboring countries but also emmanuel  macron is has acknowledged that there is  a change here in west africa there have  been several cues that have taken place  uh and there is an increase in  anti-french sentiment so it's not as  easy as just taking troops from one  country and putting it putting them in  another france would really have to  consider what impact uh that will have  on the political politics in the region  all right i said thanks very much indeed  for that that's a big reporting there  thanks a lot
 

